      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I wouldn't say it leads to \"cursed setups\". You just need a `PlayerObject` with a `Persistence` component, then you can always access it through `player.GetPlayerObjects()`. And just have a function on the behavior that when you apply a new URL, you Synchronize it (since ideally it should be set to Manual sync).\n\nBut yeah would still be nice if it was `PlayerData` serialized too, odd that it isn't (though I haven't checked if that's still the case at the time if this writing).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-10-12T15:23:02.474Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Issue:\n\nCurrently Player Data doesn't support VRCUrl, which makes using persistence for URL Input Fields really annoying to do.\n\nCurrently the only way to store a VRCUrl is with PlayerObjects, which can often lead to some quite cursed setup.\n\n# Suggestion:\n\nAdd VRCUrl to the support data types of Player Data, this would allow us to more easily store and access them.",
